From: Zakk <zakk@gentoozh.org>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] nl80211: log a failed station add at the info level

Local patch for diagnosing the AP MLD "Could not add STA to kernel
driver" loop: ap_sta_re_add() and add_associated_sta() log that line at
the info level, but the kernel error behind it was printed only at the
debug level, and running hostapd at debug floods the persistent syslog.

Print the command (NEW_STATION, SET_STATION, ADD_LINK_STA or
MODIFY_LINK_STA), the station address, the link ID (-1 when the request
names no link) and the error at the info level instead. Logging only, no
change in behaviour.

Signed-off-by: Zakk <zakk@gentoozh.org>
---
--- a/src/drivers/driver_nl80211.c
+++ b/src/drivers/driver_nl80211.c
@@ -6751,8 +6751,10 @@ static int wpa_driver_nl80211_sta_add(vo
 	ret = send_and_recv_cmd(drv, msg);
 	msg = NULL;
 	if (ret)
-		wpa_printf(MSG_DEBUG, "nl80211: %s result: %d (%s)",
-			   cmd_string, ret, strerror(-ret));
+		wpa_printf(MSG_INFO,
+			   "nl80211: %s STA " MACSTR " link_id=%d failed: %d (%s)",
+			   cmd_string, MAC2STR(params->addr),
+			   params->mld_link_id, ret, strerror(-ret));
 	if (ret == -EEXIST)
 		ret = 0;
 fail:
